WEBVTT

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.900
I can't see anything! There's no way I can control the plane now!

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.280
It's impossible to deliver goods to such place! We will fall at this rate!

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.990
Plus, there is nowhere to land in this kind of location! Huh?!

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:18.910
That's…

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:30.550
What on earth is going on? I can't believe Semimaru and Kurage would be defeated!

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:38.260
Don't worry, ka! As long as we, the pest brothers, are here, everything will be fine, ka!

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:42.730
Although Yuma and Ryouga still bother me quite a bit, Kaito is still nowhere to be found…

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.230
Does that bother you, ka? Perfect!

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:52.690
I resent the gigantic Monsters the most, ka!

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.400
I am counting on you, Mosquito Ninja.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:04.870
Good. There's no abnormality anywhere in Heartland City today! Great, great! Thanks a million!

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.960
Yuma, are you planning to keep patrolling like this?

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:14.380
Of course! Those Barian guys will appear again for sure! I absolutely cannot lose!

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:21.100
Yuma... You're fine even without Astral?

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.350
<i>We part ways here, Yuma.</i>

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:29.310
Yuma...?

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.150
What are you saying? Your arrival is worth the efforts of hundreds!

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.160
Even with the Barians here, III-

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.280
To summarize, has Yuma-<i>kun</i> recovered yet?

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.330
Cat... I hope he already got over it.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:45.620
But...

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:53.000
It's here, or not! Yuma! Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:53.000
Tokunosuke?! Guys!

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.550
It's good, or not! It's ready, or not!

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.260
You idiot!

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.890
Why are you guys here?

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.640
Like I said, I already finished the preparations, or not!

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.600
Preparations?

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:15.570
How's this, or not? The grave I made for Astral.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:22.200
I found some pretty glasses from the trash plant nearby. I picked them up and made this.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.620
What are you thinking making a grave?

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.040
What else could it be? For the funeral of Astral, of course!

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:32.040
H-Hold on!

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:37.090
Funerals are something very important, or not. It allows the living to sort out their minds, or not.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:42.340
Why you...you...Tokunosuke! Knock it off already!

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.310
Try thinking about how Yuma feels for a change!

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.350
Damn you!

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.610
Shut up, or not!

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:54.980
Y-You...

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.400
That's right, or not. I was quite sad as well, or not.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:06.120
Although unlike Yuma, we can’t communicate with Astral, or not...

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:11.870
But Astral is my...no, our friend!

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.000
Everyone was saved because of Astral, or not!

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:21.760
If Astral hadn't been here... I wouldn't have...I wouldn't have been able to get along with you guys!

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.340
The same applies to me...

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.430
Me as well.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:29.730
Me too...

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.400
Astral...

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:37.440
Me as well. Everyone here has received help from Astral before.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:44.110
That’s why...this funeral was prepared for my sake! I have to host it, even it consists of only myself, or not!

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.450
Yuma, your granny said it's time for dinner.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.000
Yuma...

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.590
Astral...

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.390
I'm in such a good mood after our Duels today!

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:11.560
That's rare from you.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:19.480
Whatever you say. No matter what, about that, 
Astral...Uh, no, I mean...

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.860
As I figured, I can't take this card out.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.030
<i>That's right, Yuma.</i>

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.790
A-Astral...!

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:42.050
How is Yuma doing?

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:46.180
As a Duelist, Yuma is already topnotch.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:54.520
Astral helped Yuma improve really well. But after losing Astral, now Yuma has lost his confidence.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.850
Can he still get a hold of himself?

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:01.280
I have no idea. But since it’s Yuma we're talking, I'm sure...

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:08.030
It seems we made no mistake when selecting the target.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.080
As expected from you, Kaito. It's all thanks to you.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.660
Do you really want to go, Chris?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:22.130
Yes. This experiment is extremely dangerous. We absolutely cannot let Yuma be aware of this.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:52.720
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.770
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:05:56.060 --> 00:06:03.230
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:06.780
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:11.660
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:18.000
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.210
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:24.090
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:28.720
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.800
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:40.270
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:04.690
"The Stern Duelist - Dyson Sphere Upheaval!!"

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.530
Good, there's no abnormality!

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:13.950
Good, good. Heartland's very safe today too!

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:17.660
Don't tell me those Barian guys have gotten afraid of the great me?

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:19.620
I hope so.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:24.380
What's with that tone? Huh?!

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:28.670
You guys! You followed me again?!

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:32.260
Sorry, but we're really worried about you, Yuma.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:35.720
Why?! There's nothing to be worried about me!

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:40.180
Of course she meant the fact that you are still unable to accept the reality of losing Astral.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:44.610
What are you saying, III? I'm as good as ever...

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:47.230
You...haven’t noticed yourself?

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.490
Wha...what do you mean?

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:52.280
So you haven't noticed it.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:56.410
Yuma, the places that you've been patrolling every day...

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:04.750
That’s right, every single place...are the places of memorial where you Dueled together with Astral!

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.460
Ho...how can that be! That's not the case!

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.220
Even this place as well...

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.840
To summarize...

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:16.470
The location of Astral's grave...or not.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.020
Astral…

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:30.030
That's right, Yuma. You thought you already overcame the fact that Astral no longer exists.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:34.740
But it isn't true! Unconsciously, you're still searching for Astral!

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:43.120
The reason you repeatedly visit these places from your memories is because you always believe one day you'll meet Astral once again!

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.040
I...

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.260
I...

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.520
Y-Yuma!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:06.440
<i>That's right, that's the case.</i>

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.690
<i>I don’t believe it! I...</i>

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:19.280
<i>How can I believe that Astral's dead?!</i>

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:32.550
<i>Let's win.</i>

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:36.880
Astral...!

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:46.940
Yuma...hey, you'll catch a cold, Yuma!

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.150
Leave me alone!

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:55.320
Astral is definitely alive! There's no way that guy would die, therefore...

00:09:55.320 --> 00:10:03.790
Therefore...I will search him forever! Until I meet him once again!

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.460
I was waiting to hear those words.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:12.170
Yuma...alright, stand up!

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:17.420
Kai...Kaito! You...

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:18.550
Let's go!

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:21.550
You said "go"? To where?!

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:25.020
Do you have to ask? To bring Astral back, of course!

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:25.770
Huh?!

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:29.850
What do you mean? Bring back Astral...?

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.020
Wha...what is going on?

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:37.280
I will save the explanation for later, so let's get going!

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:39.740
Kaito...

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.410
Then that means Astral is still alive?

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.830
We are going to prove that.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.040
Going to prove it?

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.880
What's the ultimate goal of our battles?

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.880
Ultimate goal?

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:59.340
Did you forget about the Numeron Code?

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.590
Numeron...Code?

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:07.060
<i>This card is the fate of all the world, the power that decides everything.</i>

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:13.610
I'm afraid Astral's mission is...to find that card and use it to annihilate the Barian World.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:18.570
But if Astral is no longer here, there is no way to find Numeron Code.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:26.700
No matter how hard we resist, as long as the Barian's assaults keep up, sooner or later all of the Numbers will fall into their hands.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:33.830
In that case, they will modify the Numeron Code, and both the Astral World and this one will be destroyed.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:39.300
To stop this, we need Astral at all costs!

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:45.010
While you were depressed, V and I found the way to visit the Astral World.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:49.430
Visit the Astral World? But how are we going to do it?

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.730
The hints are in this coin!

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:57.360
Whoa! That's my father’s coin I found in the ruins!

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:03.660
Why...why do you have that? Let's see... One, two, three...

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:06.200
There's one missing! When did you...?!

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.870
Hmm. Stop rambling, will you? I just borrowed it.

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:15.540
Back to the subject, there are incredible secrets inside this coin.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:18.000
What's wrong, Kaito?

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.670
No, it's nothing...

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.730
Wha...What is this thing?!

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:41.070
It's a dimension teleportation device constructed by V and I.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.030
Dimension Teleportation Device?!

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.370
Kaito-<i>sama</i>, welcome back!

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:52.580
Astral's Different Dimension Spacecraft is able to search the Numbers from the ruins. Then why can it achieve that?

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:59.800
I speculated that the coins your father left in the ruins might contain some secrets and investigated in that direction.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:02.300
Dad's coins?

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:08.260
As result, those coins are actually the substances of the Astral World, Astrite.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.970
Astral Light?!

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:17.150
It's Astrite! It's a tiny piece of enormous energy which our world doesn't have.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:23.820
We can use this to open the gate towards the Parallel Worlds and send you to the Astral World!

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:27.030
Awe...awesome! To think you guys actually made this...

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:28.450
Kaito!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.200
V!

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:35.040
Why would you bring Yuma here?

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:40.540
Unlike you, I have no plan to coddle him.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:44.720
That's not the problem here! We are going to forcefully open the gate towards different dimensions!

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:47.260
Plus, we have no idea what will happen after that!

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:49.180
I know that!

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:52.560
V! why didn't you tell me about this?

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:57.640
The reason's quite simple. It's because I knew you would go for sure after I informed you about it.

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:02.150
Isn't that obvious?! Maybe we can get Astral back!

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:06.650
You have no idea how dangerous this experiment is.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:11.950
Even if you manage to enter the Astral World by chance, that's a completely unknown world,

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:17.580
and we have no idea what's going to happen next. In the worst case scenario, you might not be able to come back alive.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.840
Tha...that doesn't matter! I...I just...

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:29.470
Chris! It's definitely no coincidence that Yuma's father left those coins in the ruins.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:38.140
If he had expected everything that has happened so far, then those seven coins must be a messages to summon Yuma to the Astral World!

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:47.110
If so, Astral has to still be alive! That’s right, Astral is still alive! He's definitely alive!!

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.120
<i>I'll search until I meet him once again!</i>

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:56.660
I beg you too!

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:01.880
Yuma is the only one who can bring Astral back, so...

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.170
Kotori...

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.300
Please, V, let me go!

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:12.470
Then please get ready to set off, Yuma.

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:20.270
Listen, Yuma. We will open the gate towards the Astral World and deliver you to that place.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:28.150
But we have no idea how long this gate will last. If this closes, we can't guarantee your return.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:35.080
Right! Kotori! Don't worry, I will definitely bring Astral back!

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.410
Do it, Orbital!!

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.710
Affirmative!

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:45.340
We apply high voltage to the configured Astrite inside the device in order to let it release energy.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:51.760
By charging that energy and releasing it all at once, we can use it to open the gate towards Astral World.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:56.140
Yuma, please stay there during the charging period, and do not move an inch!

00:15:56.140 --> 00:16:02.730
We can only extract the energy from Astrite once, which means there is only one chance to open the gate!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:03.270
Got it!

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:11.700
Energy charging reaching 40%! 45...50...55...Huh?

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.320
What?! A blackout?

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:16.830
Of all the times!

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:22.290
Not good, Kaito! If the blackout continues, then this operation will fail!

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.290
Orbital, use your power!

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:27.590
My own?!

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:28.750
Hurry up and do it!

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.420
Please, Orbital!

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.880
A-A-Affirmative...

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:36.640
Well then, I will do it.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:41.640
Orbital!

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.560
Now we have insured the emergency electric power source for the device.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:53.490
Yuma Tsukumo, V, Kaito... How dare you try to visit the Astral World!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:56.660
You think yours truly will let that happen, ka?

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.490
You're...a Barian!

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:00.950
So this blackout is also your doing, yes?

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.330
Damn you Barians!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:12.340
Don’t move, Yuma! We still need a little bit time to complete the charging with Orbital’s energy. I will protect this place!

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:19.260
That’s right. Before his departure,
 we won't let you lay a finger on him!

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.850
V... Kaito...

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:31.070
How interesting. Then as you wish, I shall defeat you guys first, ka!

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:34.820
Mosquito Style Ninja Art!

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.200
Mosquito Ring Formation of Undead Corpses!

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:42.790
Inside this field, my Life be doubled, and your Life will be halved!

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.790
A Handicap Duel, eh?

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:45.960
Fine with me.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:49.250
I...hate the gigantic things the most!

00:17:55.010 --> 00:18:00.680
Especially you guys, the Duelists who control gigantic Monsters, ka!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.730
So that's your real form, huh?

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.310
V, take this!

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:11.320
This card is...

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:14.280
Please use that!

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:17.740
Yuma, I will take good care of the feelings you sent to me!

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:22.950
Kaito, I never thought a day would come where we Dueled side by side.

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:26.290
Just don't drag me down, Chris.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:30.830
Don't get ahead of yourself. Who is the one taught you about Dueling?

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:33.840
Apprentices are destined to surpass their mentors.

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:37.090
Then let me take a look at that power!

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:39.890
Duel Mode! Photon Change!

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:45.220
Duel Disk, set!

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:51.150
We're playing by Battle Royale rules! Are you prepared, ka?!

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:52.020
Duel!!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.820
My turn! Draw!

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:06.410
I special summon Deep Space Cruiser Nine! This Monster can be Special Summoned by sending one Machine-Type Monster from my hand to the Graveyard!

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.250
Then I activate a magic card, Hologram Projection!

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:19.550
By targeting one Monster on the field, this card is placed on the Monster Zone with the same Level, Attack Power, and Defense Power!

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:25.310
I target Deep Space Cruiser Nine and Special Summon a Hologram Projection to the field!

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:28.310
Oh! He's got two Level Nines!

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:34.310
I Overlay the Level Nine Deep Space Cruiser Nine and Hologram Projection!

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:37.860
I build the Overlay Network with these two Monsters!

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.990
Xyz Summon!

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:44.450
Come forth, Number 9!

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:50.580
The fate that I carry, swallow the entire galaxy and descend as a gigantic Earth!

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:53.960
Dyson Sphere the Canopy Star!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:58.340
That Monster is ridiculously huge!

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:04.850
According to the rule for a Battle Royale, each player cannot attack during their very first turn. I end my turn with that!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.930
My turn! Draw!

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:16.650
I Special Summon Photon Slasher! When there is no Monster on my field, I can Special Summon this card!

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:20.530
Then I Normal Summon Photon Chargeman!

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:25.950
Once per turn, this card can double its Attack Power until the end of my next turn!

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:29.240
I release both Monsters with 2000 or more Attack Points!

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:31.290
I Special Summon this Monster!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:34.960
The embodiment of light, descend now!

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:38.420
Come forth, Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.680
I end my turn with that.

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:48.100
So they appeared right away, the Dyson Sphere and the Galaxy-Eyes.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:51.850
Here I come, ka! My turn! Draw!

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.230
I Summon Army Mosquito Blood Force!

00:20:55.730 --> 00:21:04.860
When this card is Summoned successfully, I can add a new Army Mosquito Blood Force from my deck to my hand!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:11.620
Then I activate a Magic Card! Mosquito School Ninja Secret Art of Army Mosquito March!

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:19.960
I can Special Summon two Army Mosquito Monsters from my hand! Come out, the new Blood Forces!

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:21.920
He's got three Level Twos!

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.220
So he's also going to...?

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:28.930
I Overlay the three Level Two Army Mosquito Blood Forces!

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:33.850
I use these three Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:36.520
Xyz Summon!

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:40.860
Come forth, Number 2!

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:44.990
The shadow that passes through the silence of night!

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:50.200
Shadow Mosquito Ninja of Science!

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:52.450
Zero Attack Points?!

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.450
But where is the Monster?

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:57.040
We can't see that guy's Monster!

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:58.790
How...how can that be?!

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:01.880
My Monster's right in front of you.

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:09.220
Let me show you that largeness doesn't equal power...KA!

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:23.730
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:26.280
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:27.490
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:28.910
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:31.780
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:34.290
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:36.830
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:37.910
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:37.910 --> 00:22:38.960
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:42.340
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:44.670
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:44.670 --> 00:22:47.800
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:50.010
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:53.010
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:54.970
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:56.350
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:58.230
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.520 --> 00:23:02.520
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:02.690 --> 00:23:07.610
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.610 --> 00:23:08.860
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:12.870
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:18.250
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:19.460
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:23.590
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:25.750
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.960
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:43.940
Kaito and V's Tag Duel has finally kicked off!

00:23:43.940 --> 00:23:49.690
While two of them are cautionary about their opponent's invisible Number, a sudden change occurred to Kaito's body!

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:52.410
He doesn't know where his Monster is located!

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:54.820
Just a little more until the energy finishes charging!

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:56.280
Illusion Counter, you say?!

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:58.080
Why are you helping the Barians?!

00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:00.410
Stop it, V! Kaito isn't your enemy!

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:03.120
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:06.090
"Kaito in Frenzy: The Ultimate Showdown Between Mentor and Apprentice!!"

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:08.550
This is...the bond of Duelists!
